  "Comments": "Dissolved alumina of the Bayer liquor as sodium aluminate NaAl(OH)4. Formation enthalpy -1700.4 kJ/mol, DERIVED so that gibbsite + NaOH -> NaAl(OH)4 takes the heat of digestion of gibbsite, 252.3 kJ/kg or 19.7 kJ/mol (Langa 1985, through SysCAD), with the gibbsite and NaOH of the DWSIM electrolyte database. Heat capacity the sum of gibbsite and NaOH (Neumann-Kopp). The liquid density is a placeholder that the Bayer Liquors package replaces. Non-volatile, never precipitates (no melting point): the gibbsite precipitation is the reverse reaction.",
